# SPDX-License-Identifier: MPL-2.0
# Intentfile (A2ML Canonical) — north-star contractile for panoply
# Author: Jonathan D.A. Jewell <j.d.a.jewell@open.ac.uk>
#
# Paired runner: intend.ncl
# Verb:          intend
#
# Semantics: North-star contractile. Declares BOTH concrete committed
#            next-actions AND horizon aspirations the project wishes to
#            become. Two sections share one file because they answer
#            the same question at different ranges:
#              [[intents]] — "we WILL do this; track progress"
#                            status: declared → in_progress → done |
#                                    deferred | retired
#              [[wishes]]  — "we WISH this were true; revisit later"
#                            status: declared → in_progress → achieved |
#                                    abandoned
#                            grouped by horizon: near / mid / far.
#            Non-gating — this is a report, not a gate. See the `must`
#            contractile for hard gates.

@abstract:
North-star contractile for panoply. This repository was instantiated from
the hyperpolymath/rsr-template-repo (Rhodium Standard Repository) scaffold
and declares panoply's own committed next-actions and horizon aspirations.
@end

## Purpose

Panoply is an envelope-first language discipline: every safety claim
explicit, scoped, inspectable, and mechanically accountable. It is defined
by three artefacts — a checked Core, explicit evidence, and a
safety-envelope manifest (see docs/architecture/DESIGN-DISCIPLINE.adoc and
.machine_readable/6a2/STATE.a2ml for current status).

This repository follows the Rhodium Standard Repository governance model
(contractile files, machine-readable specifications, session bindings)
inherited from hyperpolymath/rsr-template-repo at instantiation.

## Anti-Purpose

This repository is NOT:
- The Rhodium Standard Repository template itself — it was instantiated
  FROM rsr-template-repo; see hyperpolymath/rsr-template-repo for the
  master scaffold
- Feature-complete — Core, Evidence, and Manifest are design-phase only
  (see .machine_readable/6a2/STATE.a2ml)
- A runtime library or framework by itself — it is a language-discipline
  specification with an Idris2 ABI (abi.ipkg) and a Zig FFI surface
  (src/interface/ffi/)

## If In Doubt

If you are unsure whether a change is in scope, ask. Sensitive areas:
- .machine_readable/ contractile definitions
- RSR specification files
- Governance templates
- License policy documents

## Committed Next-Actions

### core-language-spec
- description: Specify the Core — abstract syntax, typing/checking judgements, projection target
- status: declared
- notes: See .machine_readable/6a2/STATE.a2ml [route-to-mvp]

### evidence-model-spec
- description: Specify the evidence model — what counts as a witness for each guarantee class
- status: declared

### manifest-schema-spec
- description: Specify the manifest schema — how earned/un-earned guarantees are recorded per backend
- status: declared

### first-backend-contract
- description: Define the first backend contract and what guarantees it can uphold
- status: declared

### contractile-completeness
- description: Every RSR contractile has an a2ml and ncl implementation
- probe: ls .machine_readable/contractiles/*.a2ml | wc -l | grep -q "^6$"
- status: in_progress
- notes: Currently 6 contractile verbs: intend, must, trust, adjust, bust, dust

### automation-scripts
- description: All repetitive tasks have just recipes
- probe: grep -c "^# " Justfile | grep -q "^[6-9][0-9]*$"
- status: in_progress

## Wishes

### Near Horizon

#### cross-repo-validation
- description: Tooling to validate all repos against RSR spec
- horizon: near
- status: declared

#### automated-substitution
- description: Script to automate repo-specific substitution in template
- horizon: near
- status: declared

### Mid Horizon

#### formal-verification
- description: Idris2 proofs for all critical contractile invariants
- horizon: mid
- status: declared

### Far Horizon

#### ecosystem-visualization
- description: Interactive graph of all hyperpolymath repos and dependencies
- horizon: far
- status: declared
